# GitHub, not GitLab

- Source and CI are GitHub. Use `gh` and GitHub issue numbers (`#123`).
- Do not open GitLab merge requests, do not require a GitLab username, and do not write CI for GitLab shared runners.
- Conventional commits still apply (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`).
- A `macos-26` runner is required for the app. Do not point CI at an older macOS label to make a workflow green. Do not lower `MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET` to make a workflow green.
